# Pairs with RNoStrandedPrepare, and reproduces issue #4482. After a bootstrap
# the stream does not resume cleanly at the cut: records written before it that
# the origin's WAL still retains are shipped again, and nothing dedupes a saga
# record against what the snapshot already settled. A retained prepare whose
# terminal has been trimmed - the two are in different WAL partitions, trimmed
# independently - is staged on the receiver for a saga
# the snapshot already settled, and no terminal will ever consume it.
MODULE: RNoStrandedPrepareBootstrapReshipsPreCut
TARGET: RNoStrandedPrepare
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a bootstrap keeps an arbitrary subset of the pre-cut records, so a retained prepare outlives its trimmed terminal
PERTURBS: Bootstrap

--- FIND
    /\ outbox' = {}
    /\ rconn' = TRUE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: any pre-cut record still retained is shipped again.
    /\ outbox' \in SUBSET outbox
    /\ rconn' = TRUE
--- END
